=== A2.26 K6-5 clock_gettime(CLOCK_MONOTONIC) Evidence Log ===
Date: 2026-11-18
Agent: antigravity (chat A2)

1. TOLERANCE SPECIFICATION (RECORDED BEFORE FIRST RUN)
Target RTC interval: 3.000 seconds (3,000 ms, exactly 3 full CMOS RTC second transitions)
Documented Tolerance: +-500 ms (0.500 s)
Acceptable Monotonic Elapsed Range: [2,500 ms, 3,500 ms]
Rule: This tolerance was set prior to the initial test execution and will not be altered.

2. IMPLEMENTATION SUMMARY
- kernel/src/proc.rs:
  * Implemented TSC calibration against CMOS RTC: calibrate_timer() measures TSC cycles over 1.0 s of CMOS RTC.
  * Added monotonic_now() -> (u64, u64) computing (tv_sec, tv_nsec) from calibrated TSC cycles.
  * Enforced monotonicity via atomic compare-exchange on LAST_MONO_NS to guarantee time never moves backwards across rapid calls.
  * Implemented sys_clock_gettime(clock_id: u64, tp_ptr: u64) -> i64 for syscall 228.
    - Supports CLOCK_REALTIME (0), CLOCK_MONOTONIC (1), CLOCK_MONOTONIC_RAW (4), CLOCK_BOOTTIME (7).
    - Validates tp_ptr (returns -EFAULT / -14 on null or invalid memory).
    - Validates clock_id (returns -EINVAL / -22 on unknown clock ID).
    - Writes LinuxTimespec (16 bytes: tv_sec, tv_nsec) via copy_to_user.
  * Added Ring 3 payload clock_monotonic_user_entry executing 1,000 consecutive clock_gettime(CLOCK_MONOTONIC) calls.
    - Verifies syscall return 0, tv_nsec < 1_000_000_000, and non-decreasing monotonic time.
    - Exits 95 on success.
- kernel/src/trustselftest.rs:
  * Added Check 15a: Ring 3 clock_monotonic process executes 1,000 calls without going backwards (exit 95).
  * Added Check 15b: Over at least 3 seconds (3 full CMOS RTC ticks), monotonic clock agrees with CMOS RTC within documented tolerance (+-500 ms).
  * Added Check 15c: sys_clock_gettime argument validation (unknown clock -> -EINVAL, null ptr -> -EFAULT).

